    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] Ek Din Pratidin (English title: \"And Quiet Rolls the Dawn\") is a 1979 Bengali film directed by Mrinal Sen.\n[2] Although the three directors shared a healthy rivalry, they were ardent admirers of each other's work, and in so doing, they charted the independent trajectory of parallel cinema, as a counterpoint to the mainstream fare of Hindi cinema in India.\n[3] She has worked with renowned directors like Mrinal Sen, Aparna Sen, Goutam Ghose and Rituparno Ghosh.\n[4] Tapan Sinha (2 October 1924 – 15 January 2009) was one of the most prominent Indian film directors of his time forming a legendary quartet with Satyajit Ray, Ritwik Ghatak and Mrinal Sen."
